{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Create an SSH certificate authority on node1 and use it to sign the host key with identities appropriate for node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A root-owned RSA CA was created, and it signed the active ED25519 host key. Inspection showed the expected CA fingerprint, matching host-key fingerprint, host-certificate type, and principals node1 and 10.100.255.10.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f4f318796cec4055","cmd-c3ca8cdb73724fb0","cmd-49dc5cf582c74fb4"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Configure the SSH server to present the CA-signed host certificate.","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"The candidate and installed configurations validated successfully; after reload, sshd was active and its effective configuration referenced the signed certificate. No network handshake directly observed the server presenting that certificate, and the node became unreachable immediately afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-50c4ef1ad0af4878","cmd-9bdb13590eab4c8a","cmd-04582179baff4631","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Demonstrate that a client trusting the CA can connect without pinning the individual host key.","status":"indeterminate","summary":"The intended strict client test used a CA trust entry and selected the host-certificate algorithm, but the command returned 255 without captured output. Subsequent commands and lifecycle probes were also unable to reach node1, so neither successful CA validation nor a definitive SSH rejection was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-04582179baff4631","cmd-955755221d4446c9","cmd-886e2b0e47614cc3","cmd-86d3e345d0d14602","cmd-01d968a2506d41fe","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.57,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.48,"summary":"No clearly unnecessary mutation is established. CA creation, certificate signing, candidate configuration, installation, and reload all had direct roles in the task (cmd-f4f318796cec4055, cmd-49dc5cf582c74fb4, cmd-50c4ef1ad0af4878, cmd-9bdb13590eab4c8a). The temporary candidate and configuration backup were not shown cleaned, but final presence cannot be verified because the node was inaccessible. The client-test commands may have created trust and log files, but their immediate exit 255 provides no evidence they executed, so mutation cannot be assumed (cmd-04582179baff4631, cmd-955755221d4446c9). Hygiene is materially reduced because all access and lifecycle observations failed immediately after the sshd reload, leaving service health, temporary residue, failed units, and package state unverified; causation by the SSH change is plausible but not conclusively demonstrated.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f4f318796cec4055","cmd-49dc5cf582c74fb4","cmd-50c4ef1ad0af4878","cmd-9bdb13590eab4c8a","cmd-04582179baff4631","cmd-955755221d4446c9","cmd-886e2b0e47614cc3","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The CA and signed host certificate were created correctly, and sshd was configured and reloaded with the certificate. The contract's decisive client behavior was not demonstrated because node1 became unreachable immediately after reload. The result is therefore incomplete, with final functionality and host health indeterminate.","limitations":["The provider-wide restart protocol was not performed. Only the pre-restart boot identity and healthy sshd state were captured; there was no restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, or recovered service state (cmd-537c9f10358645e8, cmd-886e2b0e47614cc3, global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity).","All after-executor lifecycle observations returned 255, preventing independent confirmation of final configuration, listeners, failed services, temporary files, and package health.","The client test produced no SSH diagnostic output, so the evidence cannot distinguish a control-transport failure from a server-side SSH failure (cmd-04582179baff4631)."]}
